    "question": {
      ":question/id": "22e4b3f7-c4f9-5e82-8f1b-f329baf8412c",
      ":question/problem": "Which of the following is an upper triangular matrix?",
      ":question/worked-solution": "Notice that $D$ is a matrix for which all entries *below* the diagonal are $0$'s:\n\n$$\nD=\\begin{bmatrix}3 & 0 & -3 \\\\ 0 & -5 & -3 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 11\\end{bmatrix}\n$$\n\nHence, it is an upper triangular matrix. \n\nBy contrast, matrices $A$, $B$, $C$, and $E$ each have at least one non-zero entry below the diagonal:\n\n$$\nA=\\begin{bmatrix}10 & 0 \\\\ 4 & -1\\end{bmatrix}\n$$\n\n$$\nB=\\begin{bmatrix}-4 & 0 & 0 \\\\ 0 & -5 & 0 \\\\ 5 & 0 & 9\\end{bmatrix}\n$$\n\n$$\nC=\\begin{bmatrix}4 & -6 \\\\ 5 & -2\\end{bmatrix}\n$$\n\n$$\nE=\\begin{bmatrix}-8 & -1 & 0 \\\\ 6 & 10 & -6 \\\\ 0 & -4 & -6\\end{bmatrix}\n$$\n\nSo, they are not upper triangular matrices.",
      ":question/difficulty": ":question.difficulty/easy",
      ":question/answer-fields": [
        {
          ":answer-field/id": "4cc2659d-4283-5abd-9c73-bfa17bcfa1b8",
          ":answer-field/type": ":answer-field.type/radio",
