    "question": {
      ":question/id": "93c399b2-ca58-52e5-af6f-685c9370b0c0",
      ":question/problem": "Which of the following is an upper triangular matrix?",
      ":question/worked-solution": "Notice that $B$ is a matrix for which all entries *below* the diagonal are $0$'s:\n\n$$\nB=\\begin{bmatrix}1 & 1 & 6 \\\\ 0 & -2 & 8 \\\\ 0 & 0 & -7\\end{bmatrix}\n$$\n\nHence, it is an upper triangular matrix. \n\nBy contrast, matrices $A$, $C$, $D$, and $E$ each have at least one non-zero entry below the diagonal:\n\n$$\nA=\\begin{bmatrix}5 & 0 & 0 \\\\ 0 & -8 & 0 \\\\ 6 & 0 & -5\\end{bmatrix}\n$$\n\n$$\nC=\\begin{bmatrix}8 & 0 \\\\ -3 & -8\\end{bmatrix}\n$$\n\n$$\nD=\\begin{bmatrix}-3 & 0 \\\\ 3 & -1\\end{bmatrix}\n$$\n\n$$\nE=\\begin{bmatrix}-3 & -8 & -1 \\\\ -2 & -11 & 8 \\\\ 9 & 0 & -5\\end{bmatrix}\n$$\n\nSo, they are not upper triangular matrices.",
