    "question": {
      ":question/id": "08c3c776-15ce-5d30-ab1f-ef3e48b8c153",
      ":question/problem": "Which of the following is a lower triangular matrix?",
      ":question/worked-solution": "Notice that $D$ is a matrix for which all entries *above* the diagonal are $0$'s:\n\n$$\nD=\\begin{bmatrix}-4 & 0 & 0 \\\\ -11 & -11 & 0 \\\\ 1 & 0 & 7\\end{bmatrix}\n$$\n\nHence, it is a lower triangular matrix. \n\nBy contrast, matrices $A$, $B$, $C$, and $E$ each have at least one non-zero entry above the diagonal:\n\n$$\nA=\\begin{bmatrix}11 & 3 \\\\ 0 & 9\\end{bmatrix}\n$$\n\n$$\nB=\\begin{bmatrix}-2 & 0 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 4 & -5 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 4\\end{bmatrix}\n$$\n\n$$\nC=\\begin{bmatrix}5 & -6 \\\\ 6 & 5\\end{bmatrix}\n$$\n\n$$\nE=\\begin{bmatrix}2 & -9 & 0 \\\\ -7 & -4 & -4 \\\\ -10 & 0 & 2\\end{bmatrix}\n$$\n\nSo, they are not lower triangular matrices.",
      ":question/difficulty": ":question.difficulty/easy",
      ":question/answer-fields": [
        {
          ":answer-field/id": "2bc1ec92-a20b-5f60-8b8b-453e1a6a6a4b",
          ":answer-field/type": ":answer-field.type/radio",
          ":answer-field/choices": [
            {
              ":answer/id": "01e0479c-a8b8-57c4-9fab-9180acdc4f71",
              ":answer/type": ":answer.type/math",
              ":answer/value": "B=\\begin{bmatrix}-2 & 0 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 4 & -5 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 4\\end{bmatrix}"
