      ":question/problem": "Which of the following is a lower triangular matrix?",
      ":question/worked-solution": "Notice that $E$ is a matrix for which all entries *above* the diagonal are $0$'s:\n\n$$\nE=\\begin{bmatrix}3 & 0 \\\\ -11 & -8\\end{bmatrix}\n$$\n\nHence, it is a lower triangular matrix. \n\nBy contrast, matrices $A$, $B$, $C$, and $D$ each have at least one non-zero entry above the diagonal:\n\n$$\nA=\\begin{bmatrix}-11 & 8 \\\\ 0 & -2\\end{bmatrix}\n$$\n\n$$\nB=\\begin{bmatrix}2 & 2 \\\\ 0 & 5\\end{bmatrix}\n$$\n\n$$\nC=\\begin{bmatrix}0 & -7 \\\\ -5 & -3\\end{bmatrix}\n$$\n\n$$\nD=\\begin{bmatrix}3 & -11 \\\\ -4 & 8\\end{bmatrix}\n$$\n\nSo, they are not lower triangular matrices.",
      ":question/difficulty": ":question.difficulty/easy",
