    "question": {
      ":question/id": "a599ba50-e3a3-5f7a-a7e2-3226d8870b58",
      ":question/problem": "Which of the following is an upper triangular matrix?",
      ":question/worked-solution": "Notice that $B$ is a matrix for which all entries *below* the diagonal are $0$'s:\n\n$$\nB=\\begin{bmatrix}-5 & -6 & 11 \\\\ 0 & 10 & -9 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 11\\end{bmatrix}\n$$\n\nHence, it is an upper triangular matrix. \n\nBy contrast, matrices $A$, $C$, $D$, and $E$ each have at least one non-zero entry below the diagonal:\n\n$$\nA=\\begin{bmatrix}7 & 0 & 0 \\\\ 0 & -6 & 0 \\\\ 0 & -5 & -6\\end{bmatrix}\n$$\n\n$$\nC=\\begin{bmatrix}-7 & 0 \\\\ -2 & -11\\end{bmatrix}\n$$\n\n$$\nD=\\begin{bmatrix}3 & 0 \\\\ 4 & 9\\end{bmatrix}\n$$\n\n$$\nE=\\begin{bmatrix}-8 & -11 & 6 \\\\ -6 & 4 & 4 \\\\ 0 & 11 & -2\\end{bmatrix}\n$$\n\nSo, they are not upper triangular matrices.",
      ":question/difficulty": ":question.difficulty/easy",
      ":question/answer-fields": [
        {
          ":answer-field/id": "fec8dd3e-1ace-544e-a665-d2b6725b480a",
